{"_id":"68a736248ec3d8323af19d3f","nodeId":"L6RMExeqi9501y-eCHDt1","roadmapSlug":"linux","createdAt":"2025-08-21T15:07:16.516Z","description":"# Permissions\n\nLinux permissions control file and directory access for users, groups, and others with read, write, and execute types. Commands include `chmod` (change permissions), `chown` (change owner), and `chgrp` (change group). Proper permission management is crucial for system security and organization. Essential for maintaining controlled access to system resources.","resources":[{"type":"article","title":"Understanding Linux File Permissions","url":"https://linuxize.com/post/understanding-linux-file-permissions/","_id":"6a4cfc02b3c5c89452719e7f"},{"type":"article","title":"Linux File Permissions","url":"https://linuxhandbook.com/linux-file-permissions/","_id":"6a4cfc02b3c5c89452719e80"},{"type":"article","title":"Linux Permissions of Files","url":"https://labex.io/tutorials/linux-permissions-of-files-270252","_id":"6a4cfc02b3c5c89452719e81"},{"type":"video","title":"Linux File Permissions in 5 Minutes","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=LnKoncbQBsM","_id":"6a4cfc02b3c5c89452719e82"}],"updatedAt":"2026-07-07T13:15:46.443Z","lessonPacks":[],"paidResources":[],"contribution":"https://github.com/kamranahmedse/developer-roadmap/tree/master/roadmaps/linux/content/L6RMExeqi9501y-eCHDt1.md"}